1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,860
I kicked a pebble and it
flew off into the clouds.

3
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:29,360
To the gym teacher who was out jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
it's for real, there's no other way.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
the streets that never change,
no matter what,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,900
the ponzu will give it to you, won't it.

11
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,940
Stuffing yakitori in my mouth.

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,620
Is it even worth looking at?

13
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:57,500
Of the pointy hat...

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,060
From the waterworks,
past the big power lines, the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, it ends with something dropped

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
A magazine comes out, and happiness again.

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,280
I'm a fool who only
realized after losing it.

18
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,200
The two-person police box

19
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:52,240
Mmmm

20
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:52,660
Mm

21
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:52,880
Mm

22
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:53,000
Mm

23
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,480
Mm

24
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:53,500
Mm

25
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:53,520
Mm

26
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:53,540
Mm

27
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:53,820
Mm

28
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,080
You got mail.

29
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:19,700
Damn, I forgot I set it up myself.

30
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,620
Well, I'm wide awake now, at least.

31
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:24,580
It's all because of the Chief,

32
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:27,660
you idiot, always coming in late!

33
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:31,200
If you're late tomorrow,
you're fired on the spot, got it?

34
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:36,240
Since I haven't bathed in a while anyway,

35
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,000
guess I'll wash my hair too.

36
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:47,060
Good morning, Reiko-san.

37
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:47,960
Morning.

38
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,640
I just got a call,

39
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,980
and Terai-san says he's
out sick with a cold.

40
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,960
That's right.
He did look listless yesterday.

41
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,360
So that means it's just
me and Ryo-chan today.

42
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,980
Chief Ohara and Nakagawa-san,

43
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:07,560
Nakagawa-san said he was going to Europe on vacation,
didn't he?

44
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,640
Right.

45
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:11,380
The Chief is at a wedding, I think.

46
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:16,040
So that means we're stuck with that gorilla man all day,
isn't it?

47
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,920
I suppose it does.

48
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:23,360
It's dangerous, spending all day with a savage,
perverted middle-aged gorilla like that.

49
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:27,040
That's right. Today we'll go
to the station to back you up.

50
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,780
Don't worry about it.

51
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:35,800
Grandma and he are beyond men and women.
We're just friends who get along well.

52
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,460
But...

53
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:39,960
Really, it's fine. I'm heading out now.

54
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:53,380
Let's see,
the relatively newest underwear is

55
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:53,860
I see.

56
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:01,280
Alright,
this shirt has the least dirt on it.

57
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,400
Uh-oh.

58
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,340
I'm late again. Hurry, hurry!

59
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,960
Dage dage dage!

60
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:22,040
Ryo-chan, what are you doing?

61
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:24,920
The Chief's in the back room?

62
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,554
Ryo-chan,

63
00:05:26,604 --> 00:05:30,120
You said yesterday that the Chief is off today for a wedding,
didn't you?

64
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,540
Seriously?!

65
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,380
Geez, you never listen to anyone.

66
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:36,807
Hey, I panicked for nothing.

67
00:05:36,857 --> 00:05:38,660
I'm going back to bed.

68
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:41,540
No way, Ryo-chan,
there are only two of us today.

69
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:44,060
Nakagawa and Terai are around, aren't they?

70
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,978
Kei-chan's in Europe,

71
00:05:46,028 --> 00:05:48,160
Terai's out sick.

72
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:52,120
So it's just me and Reiko today?

73
00:05:57,020 --> 00:06:00,100
So it's just Ryo-san and Reiko-san,
alone together

74
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:04,660
Well, Reiko doesn't seem to
mind that gorilla of a man,

75
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,220
so I don't think there's
anything to worry about.

76
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:08,280
Maybe so for Reiko,

77
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,620
but the other party is Ryotsu, after all.

78
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:15,900
Come on, come on!

79
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:18,420
I can't just sit here!

80
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:19,940
Maria-chan

81
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,460
Ow

82
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:24,620
What's wrong, Reiko?

83
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:26,980
I think an eyelash got in my eye.

84
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,040
Geez, what a pain.

85
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,740
Sit down, I'll take a look.

86
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:35,440
Come on, open your eye.

87
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,640
Be gentle, okay?

88
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,720
I know, I know.

89
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:43,520
There it is, there it is!

90
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,640
Ryo-chan, that hurts!

91
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:48,260
Sorry, sorry, Reiko.

92
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,700
Don't make such a fuss.

93
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,120
My bad.

94
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,240
Don't be so nervous.

95
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,980
Okay, let's start over.

96
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,260
R-R-Ryo-sama!

97
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,540
Ryo!

98
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,760
Hehehe!

99
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,220
Uuugh!

100
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,300
I'm terribly sorry!

101
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:12,842
No way,

102
00:07:12,892 --> 00:07:16,620
I didn't think you were
actually removing an eyelash...

103
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,940
Seriously, that's a total misunderstanding!

104
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,040
Anyway,
why the hell are you coming to the box?!

105
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,740
Well, that's...

106
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:28,100
I get it. Komachi and the others must
have filled your head with nonsense, right?

107
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:35,880
Nothing's going to happen just because Ryo-chan and I are alone,
you know.

108
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,300
Hey, Ryo-chan.

109
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:38,420
Of course.

110
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:42,140
It was my fault for doubting you, Lord Ryo.

111
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,100
I am truly sorry.

112
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:47,560
Lord Ryo, please forgive this foolish me.

113
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:50,340
Got it, now just go home.

114
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:54,100
Lord Ryo, so you've come to dislike me.

115
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:59,560
No, no, that's not it.
You have your own work to do, right?

116
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,640
Well, yes, but...

117
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:05,760
With you hanging around like that,
I can't get any work done.

118
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:09,380
Right, if Maria-chan were here,
you'd be worried sick, wouldn't you?

119
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:14,560
Understood. I'll believe you, Ryo-san.

120
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,140
So it wasn't me, then?

121
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,180
Well then, I'll be taking my leave.

122
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,220
Alright, done.

123
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:34,280
I'll go on patrol to kill some time.

124
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,560
Oh shit, oh shit.

125
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,740
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

126
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:41,160
The model shop owner's
here to collect a debt.

127
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,860
Reiko, get rid of him for me.

128
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:46,900
This is your own mess, Ryo-chan.
Deal with it yourself.

129
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:49,580
I'm in a bind until payday.

130
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:51,340
Please, for pity's sake!

131
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,100
Reiko-san, where's Ryo-san?

132
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,900
Uh uh

133
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,740
It's no use hiding it.

134
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,439
I heard it from Komachi-chan,

135
00:09:07,489 --> 00:09:10,500
so I know you're on duty
alone with Ryo-san today.

136
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,900
That Komachi,
always saying unnecessary things.

137
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:17,740
Ryo-chan went out on patrol a while ago,
you know.

138
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:21,360
You seem a bit uneasy, Reiko-san.

139
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,420
N-no, that's not true at all.

140
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,400
That locker looks suspicious.

141
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,780
There's no way he could
fit in a space that small!

142
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:39,780
I'd like to say that makes sense,

143
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:43,480
but Ryo-san will do
anything when he's cornered.

144
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,560
I was sure he was here.

145
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,760
That leaves the back room.

146
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,100
Ryo-san, it's no use hiding.

147
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:00,240
You're finally paying off
everything you owe today!

148
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,780
Here? Here? Here? Here?

149
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:02,460
Damn it.

150
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,820
He's not here.

151
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:09,980
Haah.

152
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,520
Didn't I tell you?

153
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,240
He went out on patrol.

154
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:18,100
I'll tell Ryo-chan to pay
you when he gets back, so.

155
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,540
He's gone. You can come out now.

156
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,160
I'd love to, but it's a real pain.

157
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:33,940
I can't get out like this. Help me.

158
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,700
Ryo-chan, honestly.

159
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,160
You're really a handful.

160
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:40,480
I'm pulling now.

161
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,700
Don't hold back, okay?

162
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:45,280
Don't pull my face!

163
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,100
I got out.

164
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:53,540
Thanks, Reiko.

165
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,540
What's with that get-up?

166
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:57,600
Well, my body won't go back to normal.

167
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,420
But I can still move like this.

168
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:01,360
See? See? See?

169
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:05,340
I can't go on patrol like this.

170
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:09,360
What's worst is that even if I need the toilet,
I can't pull my pants down.

171
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:11,040
What do we do, Reiko?

172
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:14,600
Right, we have to get
you back to normal somehow.

173
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,060
That's it, if we pour hot water on it...

174
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:18,760
Freeze-dried method

175
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:21,620
So you can move your legs?

176
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,740
Only my toes, though.

177
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,460
Did you hook your toes on something?

178
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:28,400
Whatever you do, don't let go!

179
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,440
Got it.

180
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,540
Thank goodness, I can grab his chin.

181
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:37,440
Hey, that tickles!
What are you planning, Reiko?

182
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,420
Just bear with it a little.

183
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:52,160


184
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:54,960
Aaaaaah!

185
00:11:57,460 --> 00:12:00,680
Thanks to you, I'm back to normal.

186
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:01,920
Ryo-chan.

187
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,220
Aaaaaah!

188
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:04,920
Ryotsu Kankichi!

189
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:07,260
What do you think you're doing to Reiko-san?

190
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,660
No, no, that's not it!

191
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,540
That's...

192
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,600
That's...

193
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,060
Today's been nothing but this kind of thing.

194
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:38,500
I-I'm sorry.

195
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,000
That's torture!

196
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,360
I-I had no idea it was something like that!

197
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:47,160
Anyone would misunderstand,
seeing that situation.

198
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:47,720
Right?

199
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,300
This is no laughing matter!

200
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,720
Ryo-chan,
hold still until I'm done treating it.

201
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,400
There, all done.

202
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:58,218
Geez,

203
00:12:58,268 --> 00:13:01,960
Thanks to you two,
I got a heel drop from Maria.

204
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,960
And the model shop guy sent
a debt collector after me!

205
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:06,860
Talk about adding insult to injury.

206
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,680
What? It's all your fault to begin with,
isn't it?

207
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,820
That's right,
your everyday behavior is just too awful.

208
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:13,960
What did you say?!

209
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:16,040
Ryo-chan, calm down, calm down.

210
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:19,040
You two came here to have lunch together,
didn't you?

211
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:20,260
That's right.

212
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,280
Okay~

213
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:29,620
Delicious.

214
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:33,680
Ryo-chan,
why don't you come over and eat too?

215
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,860
Ko-san, never mind the gorilla guy.

216
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,740
It'll ruin our lunch.

217
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:41,840
Leave him alone.
I'm not one of you lot, you know.

218
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,720
Ryo-san.

219
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:45,420
Junpei.

220
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,880
Ryo-san, it's a disaster.

221
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,800
What on earth happened?

222
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,900
That's why it's a disaster. Come on!

223
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:52,320
Got it.

224
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,220
You two, mind the box for a bit.

225
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,700
Ryo-chan, be careful.

226
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,760
Just a little more, hang in there, Ryo-san!

227
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,120
It's fine, it's fine.

228
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,020
with the utmost care.

229
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:21,320
If we handle it quickly and efficiently,

230
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,920
even this imminent crisis
will become a laughing matter.

231
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,720
Trading crisis!

232
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:28,000
Yay!

233
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,100
Yay!

234
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:30,980
Yay!

235
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:32,680
Whoa!

236
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,440
Ryo-chan!

237
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:40,540
Ryo-chan!

238
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,480
Nyah!

239
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,940
Whoa! I'm gonna do it!

240
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,080
Ha the plane's fine!

241
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:52,460
Whoa!

242
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:53,760
It's skyrocketed!

243
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:01,180
No good, it won't move.

244
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:05,100
The engine's gone bad

245
00:15:05,100 --> 00:15:07,140
Junpei, lend me the toolbox.

246
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:07,500
Right!

247
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:10,317
Okay,

248
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:13,080
it's done!

249
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,620
Whoa!

250
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:16,200
Yaah!

251
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,300
Yes!

252
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:22,160
The engine's alive, you know!

253
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,800
Here, Junpei!

254
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,140
Thanks, Ryo-san!

255
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,220
Here, have some tea.

256
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,720
Thanks.

257
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,720
Junpei and the others were really pleased,
weren't they.

258
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,727
That's good,

259
00:15:41,777 --> 00:15:45,480
tea tastes so good after a hard day's work.

260
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:49,820
What is it? Do I have something on my face?

261
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:54,160
What's this? I've been running around
with this stuck on me all along,

262
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:57,300
It's okay, nobody's going to laugh.

263
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,040
Never forgetting the heart of a child.

264
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:04,820
No, I like Ryo-chan just the way he is,
a child forever.

265
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,660
Don't tease me. Geez, what a pain.

266
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,360
Hey, this is...

267
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:12,800
Could it be...

268
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,220
And you are?

269
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:26,640
Yes, yes, long time no see,
you super-pauper.

270
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,140
Who was it again?

271
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:31,300
I-I'm the rude one, me!

272
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,340
Even if you say that...

273
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:35,120
Do you know Reiko?

274
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:38,020
Well, I can't seem to remember him either.

275
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,500
Reiko-san, it's me.

276
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:43,220
I'm the super-rich Reiji Shiratori.

277
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:47,620
Good, you remembered me.

278
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:48,840
Well, actually...

279
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:57,200
Hey, what are you gonna do about this? You left me stuck there,
so everyone completely forgot about

280
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:03,460
me! Ugh. Calm down, already. Who do
you think you're talking to, Shiratori?

281
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:12,060
Aw, don't be so mean. Mr. Super Poor. Reiko-san too. That's why I call you
"Super," dammit.

282
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:14,736
Hey, long time no see. But you,

283
00:17:14,786 --> 00:17:20,420
weren't you disowned by your father
and turned into a super poor guy?

284
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:24,160
Daddy lifted the disownment,
and I made my comeback as managing director.

285
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,740
What a softie Daddy is.
So, what do you want today?

286
00:17:28,940 --> 00:17:31,700
Good question, Mr. Super Poor.

287
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:34,000
Okay, okay, stop pointing at people.

288
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:35,300
Test moment!

289
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,920
W-what's this flower?

290
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,560
Did you bring it in that Porsche
with no sense of the season at all?

291
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,820
Don't sweat the small stuff.

292
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:54,440
Anyway, Reiko, now that I've made
my comeback as a super rich man,

293
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:57,120
I'm going to take you as my bride.

294
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:01,320
I already turned that down before, didn't I?

295
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:06,200
I can see right through you.
That's not what you really think.

296
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:10,540
You're going to become my bride.
It's destiny.

297
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:12,700
Ryo-chan.

298
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:15,420
Hey, Reiko doesn't want that,
can't you tell?

299
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:19,100
And stop that thing. It's unbearably stinky.

300
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,653
W-what do you mean, "bride"?

301
00:18:20,703 --> 00:18:24,090
The part that's a bit big is stuck,
that's the whole problem,

302
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,120
ah from up high,

303
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:29,245
Mr. Shiratori,
since we're on the subject, I'll say it,

304
00:18:29,295 --> 00:18:31,060
you came too late.

305
00:18:31,060 --> 00:18:33,940
Ugh, nyaa, this smells bad too.

306
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:36,860
I'm engaged.

307
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:38,920
Eeeeeeeeh?!

308
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:42,040
Th-that's just another joke, right?

309
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:42,780
It's true.

310
00:18:43,410 --> 00:18:45,620
Then who is this fiancé of yours?

311
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:47,840
W-well, that's...

312
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:51,180
It's this old me!

313
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,980
Yeah! That's right!

314
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:56,260
Well, that's how it is.

315
00:18:56,750 --> 00:18:59,080
Shiratori-kun, you really were too late.

316
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:03,660
We were just discussing
where to go on our honeymoon.

317
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,360
Hey, honey?

318
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,680
Yes, darling?

319
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:07,900
Wh-honey?

320
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,600
Darling.

321
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,820
I suppose Europe would be nice, right?

322
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:15,840
A trip around the world, obviously.

323
00:19:18,380 --> 00:19:20,140
No, it's absolutely strange.

324
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:21,480
What is?

325
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,200
Where?

326
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:24,680
When you think about it carefully,

327
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:26,980
no, even without thinking carefully, it is.

328
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,920
Even if heaven and earth
were turned upside down,

329
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:29,600
Reiko-san would

330
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:32,240
never fall for a super barbarian like you,

331
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,380
super pauper,

332
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,520
super stubby-legs,

333
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:36,580
super long-armed freak,

334
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:38,820
there's no way she'd fall
for a gorilla-like man!

335
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:41,280
W-well, that's my business, isn't it?

336
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:44,880
Heh heh, your flustered act
only makes it more suspicious.

337
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:48,540
Then let's see proof of that.

338
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:49,400
Proof?

339
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,820
If you're really engaged,
then right here,

340
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:55,600
let's see a passionate kiss in front of me.

341
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:56,340
What?

342
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,180
Not a peck on the cheek.

343
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:03,020
A full mouth-to-mouth smooch, got it?

344
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,460
Come on, that's in front of people!

345
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,900
If you're engaged,
you should be able to do it.

346
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:13,240
Come on, I'll even take a photo as proof.

347
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,060
Let's see you do it.

348
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:17,940
Come on, come on, come on!

349
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:18,980
Come on!

350
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:24,980
I can do it.

351
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:28,500
I can do it.

352
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:30,900
Re...

353
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:32,140
Reiko...

354
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:34,740
Wh-what?

355
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,500
Oh, right, I can do it!

356
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:38,120
Hey.

357
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:40,360
Just watch closely.

358
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:41,240
Hey.

359
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:45,240
Sorry, Reiko, could you bend down a little?

360
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:45,600
Kan?

361
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:48,340
Okay then, here I go!

362
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,960
Aaaaaah!

363
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:53,980
Aaaaaah!

364
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,620
Hold on a sec!

365
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:05,500
Excuse me, it's from Dad.

366
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,020
Hello, this is Reji.

367
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,480
The company went bankrupt.

368
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:15,200
So he's going to fall from
super-rich back to poor again?

369
00:21:15,740 --> 00:21:19,060
Mr. Shiratori, you can't be dawdling here!

370
00:21:19,060 --> 00:21:21,900
That's right,
this is a crisis for the Shiratori family!

371
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:25,260
Yes, I understand, Dad.
I'm heading over right now.

372
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,640
So, I'm afraid I have to excuse myself.

373
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:33,060
Dad!

374
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:37,480
Hey! What are you planning
to do with this flower?!

375
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:43,540
It stinks!

376
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:50,300
Hey, Reiko.

377
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:58,980
If that call from Shiratori's
father hadn't come in...

378
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:03,380
Were you really planning to kiss?

379
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:07,160
Come on, it was obviously a joke.

380
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:09,120
Yeah, right?

381
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,980
Finally, it's over.

382
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:22,660
So much happened today.

383
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:26,040
Way too much. I'm wiped out.

384
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:30,800
Ryo-chan,
how about having a meal together sometime?

385
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:34,920
Sounds good, but I...

386
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:38,400
Don't worry, it's my treat.

387
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:41,220
What's gotten into you?

388
00:22:41,220 --> 00:22:42,480
No particular reason.

389
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:45,720
Well, fine.
No reason at all, and I'm all for it.

390
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:51,920
Ahhh, it's Ryo-san!
Honda, what happened to you?

391
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:54,420
What?

392
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:55,080
Oh my.

393
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:56,920
Senpai...

394
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:59,680
What on earth is it?

395
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:02,740
Nana-chan won't even wait for me a little.

396
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:04,800
I think I've been dumped.

397
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,880
You're overthinking it.

398
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:09,340
She won't even reply to my emails.

399
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:11,500
It's all over for me.

400
00:23:12,380 --> 00:23:13,700
Hey, listen.

401
00:23:16,820 --> 00:23:17,960
Sorry.

402
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:21,440
I'd love to,
but I'm keeping Honda company tonight.

403
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,300
I'm going to hear Honda out properly.

404
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,640
Lecture.

405
00:23:27,980 --> 00:23:29,480
Come on, pull yourself together.

406
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,780
Yeah, let's go drinking.

407
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:33,860
Of course, you're treating.

408
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:34,560
Yes.

409
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:35,580
Alright.

410
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:38,180
You two shouldn't drink too much.

411
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:40,080
I'm heading out for a bit.

412
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:52,040
What? At Nakagawa's bio farm,

413
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,040
they've got too many sweet
potatoes and are in trouble?

414
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:55,480
I'll take those potatoes.

415
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:57,880
If I start a grilled sweet
potato stall with these,

416
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,440
it won't cost me a thing,
and it should turn a profit, I figure.

417
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:01,900
But just as I was thinking that,
some weird takoyaki stall

418
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:03,120
started picking a fight with me.

419
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:06,280
Next time: Clash!
The Station Front Stall War.

420
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:07,440
See you then.

421
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:10,500
Kameari, for sure!

422
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:21,060
Thank you for watching.

